#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Release gate: a strict superset of ./scripts/verify. It answers "can we
# release", never "can we merge" (AGENTS.md §Verification).
#
# INCOMPLETE BY DESIGN. The breadth checks below arrive with the work they
# cover, so this script deliberately exits non-zero rather than reporting a
# release-ready tree it has not actually verified.
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."

./scripts/verify

echo "==> release-critical quarantines"
./scripts/check-quarantines --release

cat >&2 <<'MISSING'

verify-release: INCOMPLETE — the following gates are not implemented yet:

  supported provider/version matrix       (PR4-PR6)
  packaging / install / uninstall         (M1 completion, after PR8)
  multi-platform release checks           (macOS + Linux)
  migration verification                  (PR2 onward)
  dogfood release-gate evidence           (ROADMAP.md §5)

Implement the gate with the work it covers; do not make this script pass by
removing the check.
MISSING
exit 1
